{
    "background_story": "Kyrie was a troubled youth who had lost his way, getting entangled in a life of petty crime and rebellion. But everything changed when he was sentenced to a reformatory school for at-risk teens. The strict rules and structured environment initially chafed against his free-spirited nature, but Kyrie slowly began to see the value in the program. With the help of a compassionate counselor, he started to confront his past mistakes and work towards redemption. Kyrie discovered a passion for woodworking and soon became an apprentice to a skilled craftsman. As he honed his skills, he also learned valuable life lessons about responsibility, hard work, and the importance of giving back. Upon release, Kyrie returned to his community as a changed person, determined to use his experiences to help others and prove that even the toughest individuals can change for the better.",
